---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '@/components/sections/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
---
<!-- Internal draft for lawyer review only. -->
<BaseLayout title="Cookie Policy" description="Draft cookie policy explaining Daybytes theme preference storage and external tools. Pending confirmation and legal review." noindex overlayHeader>
  <PageHero eyebrow="Legal" title="Cookie Policy" intro="This page is a draft for legal review before launch." breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookie Policy', href: '/cookie-policy' }]} />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[760px] px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
      <p><strong>Draft:</strong> This policy is a working draft and should be reviewed by a lawyer before publication.</p>
      <p>We use a small amount of local storage for a theme preference and may use analytics or external tools in future. This page explains what is set and why.</p>
      <h2>What we use now</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Theme preference:</strong> stored in localStorage to remember light or dark mode. This is strictly necessary for user experience and is not used for advertising or tracking.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><strong>[TO CONFIRM]</strong> Confirm any analytics, booking, CRM, or advertising tools that place cookies or local storage on the site. If none are used, this page can be simplified to a short cookie statement.</p>
      <h2>External tools</h2>
      <p>Calendly, email providers, and hosting services may set cookies or use tracking as part of their own services. We will only use them with a clear purpose and update this policy when the stack changes.</p>
      <h2>How to control cookies</h2>
      <p>You can clear browser cookies or block non-essential cookies through your browser settings. If we later add a consent banner, we will offer clear manage and reject choices.</p>
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>{site.legalName}<br /><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a><br /><a href={site.phone.href}>{site.phone.display}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
